{{Quote|You think this pilot acted alone? He was dispatched from the installation on Eadu. Galen Erso's facility.|Grand Moff Wilhuff Tarkin to Director Orson Krennic|<ref name="Rogue One" />}}
The '''Eadu Energy Conversion Laboratory''',<ref name="SW AB">''[[Star Wars: Absolutely Everything You Need to Know, Updated and Expanded]]''</ref> also known as the '''Tarkin Initiative R&D base''',<ref name="Helmet Collection 71">{{HelmetCollectionCite|71|Helmets}}</ref> '''Tarkin Initiative laboratory''',<ref name="UVG" /> '''Imperial kyber refinery'''<ref name="Rogue One" /> or the '''Laboratory of Conception and Implementation of the High Energies''',<ref name="Geektionary">''[[Star Wars: Geektionary: The Galaxy from A - Z]]''</ref> was a secluded [[Galactic Empire|Imperial]] research and development facility located on the [[planet]] [[Eadu]]. Guarded by the [[975th Battalion]], the installation was where the development research was done for the [[DS-1 Orbital Battle Station|Death Star's]] [[superlaser]] under the direction of [[Galen Walton Erso|Galen Erso]] as part of the [[Tarkin Initiative]]. A [[Kyber crystal research team|team]] of [[scientist]]s at the complex undertook two interconnected projects: the fusing of [[kyber crystal]] shards into larger forms and the creation and redirection of a controlled chain reaction.<ref name="UVG" /> Attached to the facility was a single-barrel [[Turret|defensive]] [[turbolaser]] [[Laser cannon|cannon]], along with a launch bay for [[TIE/ln space superiority starfighter]]s and at least 1 [[TIE/rp Reaper attack lander]] and a [[Eadu Flight Station|shuttle station]] where [[Zeta-class Heavy Cargo Shuttle|cargo shuttles]] delivered crystals for the team in specialized [[Kyber crystal container|containers]].<ref name="Rogue One" />

During [[Operation Fracture]] in [[1 BBY]],<ref name="Timelines" /><ref name="UVG" /> a [[Alliance to Restore the Republic|Rebel]] squad consisting of [[Captain]] [[Cassian Jeron Andor|Cassian Andor]], [[Jyn Erso]], [[K-2SO]], [[Bodhi Rook]], [[Baze Malbus]], and [[Chirrut Îmwe]] [[Mission to Eadu|traveled]] to the facility in a [[UT-60D U-wing starfighter/support craft]] to find Galen Erso. [[Director]] [[Orson Callan Krennic|Orson Krennic]] arrived shortly after the Rebels in his [[ST-149|Imperial shuttle]] to investigate suspicions of a Rebel sympathizer within the scientific ranks. After Erso revealed himself as the traitor, Krennic had Erso's team executed by [[death trooper]]s. The complex was then attacked by rebel [[starfighter]]s, consisting of [[T-65B X-wing starfighter]]s and [[BTL-A4 Y-wing assault starfighter/bomber]]s<ref name="Rogue One" /> from [[Blue Squadron (Rebel Alliance)|Blue Squadron]].<ref name="Grounded">{{StoryCite|story=Grounded|book=From a Certain Point of View}}</ref> In response, the base's [[Anti-aircraft cannon|defensive cannon]] and [[TIE/ln space superiority starfighter]]s were dispatched to counter the threat, only to be overwhelmed by the Alliance as Îmwe led to the turbolaser's destruction, allowing for the Rebel strike team's success. Ultimately, an alliance torpedo brought severe damages to Director Krennic's landing platform, killing several stormtroopers and mortally wounding Galen Erso, who conversed with his daughter before the remaining Rebels fled from the planet.<ref name="Rogue One" />

